  "definition": "An environmental control and life support system, or ECLSS, maintains the conditions needed for people and other living payloads inside a spacecraft or habitat. Its scope includes atmospheric composition and pressure, ventilation, carbon-dioxide and trace-contaminant removal, oxygen supply, water recovery and quality, waste handling, environmental monitoring, and interfaces to thermal control and fire detection.[^1]",
